body: "**Version:** 2026.10.23. **Scope:** core extension discovery. Low/medium agent UX.\n\nIn a dedicated small extension directory, create package.json:\n\n~~~json\n{\"name\":\"ux-probe-six\",\"version\":\"0.1.0\",\"type\":\"module\",\"peerDependencies\":{\"@unbrained/pm-cli\":\"2026.10.23\"}}\n~~~\n\nmanifest.json:\n\n~~~json\n{\"name\":\"ux-probe-six\",\"version\":\"0.1.0\",\"manifest_version\":2,\"entry\":\"./index.ts\",\"capabilities\":[\"commands\",\"schema\"]}\n~~~\n\nindex.ts:\n\n~~~ts\nimport { defineExtension } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/authoring';\nimport type { ExtensionApi } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/authoring';\nexport default defineExtension({ activate(api: ExtensionApi) {\n  api.registerCommand({ name: 'uxhello', description: 'Synthetic greeting',\n    flags: [\n      { long: '--name', value_name: 'text', default: 'agent', description: 'Name' },\n      { long: '--count', value_name: 'number', value_type: 'number',\n        value_validation: 'strict', default: 1, description: 'Count' }\n    ],\n    run: c => ({ name: c.options.name, count: c.options.count })\n  });\n}});\n~~~\n\nIn a different initialized scratch tracker, with pm meaning npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.23:\n\n~~~bash\npm install <dedicated-small-extension-dir>\npm uxhello --help\npm help uxhello --json\npm contracts --command uxhello --flags-only --json\npm contracts --command uxhello --runtime-only --schema-only --json\npm uxhello --json\n~~~\n\n**Observed:** omitted flags execute as agent/1. Text and machine help show names/arity/type but no defaults. Flag contracts and command-scoped schema omit defaults too. The published FlagDefinition.default declaration promises values are “Surfaced to runtime contracts and help output.” Strict numeric validation works; the defect is discovery metadata loss.\n\n**Expected:** include defaults in text/machine help and runtime schemas/contracts, so agents can learn omitted-flag behavior without executing a potentially mutating extension command. The tested command is harmless; this probe does not assert all extension commands are safe discovery mechanisms.\n\n**Measured cost:** text help **59.5 tokens**, flags-only contracts **1,733.25**, no-flag execution **13.75**: **three calls / 1,806.5 stdout tokens**, learning defaults only by execution. Additional machine-help/schema probes cost **287 / 827.75** without restoring them. An author can manually repeat defaults in descriptions as a workaround.\n\n**Duplicate searches:** each used gh issue list -R unbraind/pm-cli --state all --search \"<query>\" --limit 20:\n\n- extension flags default help\n- registerCommand default\n- \"extension\" \"default\" \"metadata\"\n- \"flag\" \"defaults\" \"help\"\n- \"registerFlags\" \"default\"\n- \"value_validation\" \"contracts\"\n\nNo matching report found. #719 concerns global-flag collisions; #550/#496 list accumulation; #772 rejected registrations; #1363 broader progressive discovery. None owns the concrete declared-default omission.\n\n\n\n---\nFound by an agent-UX probe of 2026.10.23 (agent seat and extension-author seat) and re-verified by the maintainer orchestrator against the globally installed 2026.10.23 before filing."
